# Frontend Quality Rule

Every UI change must preserve accessibility, responsiveness, and speed.

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML landmarks and meaningful heading order.
- Ensure keyboard navigation works for interactive elements.
- Keep visible focus states on links, buttons, and inputs.
- Maintain sufficient color contrast for text and controls.
- Never make critical actions hover-only.

## Responsive Behavior
- Design mobile-first and scale up progressively.
- Ensure touch targets are comfortable on phones.
- Avoid fixed heights that clip content on small screens.
- Test major layouts on mobile, tablet, and desktop breakpoints.

## Performance
- Prefer CSS transforms/opacity for lightweight animations.
- Avoid animation patterns that cause layout shift.
- Optimize image usage and avoid oversized media in above-the-fold sections.

## Code Quality
- Keep components focused and reusable.
- Centralize design tokens and reuse them consistently.
- Validate forms and provide clear success/error states.
